    "https://www.sdsmt.edu/student-life/support-and-services/career-services/internships-and-co-ops.html": {
      "title": "Internships and Co-ops",
      "description": "Gain Real Experience: Internships and Co-ops Offered Skip to content I am a Current Student Admitted Student Faculty/Staff Parent/Family Alumni Industry Partner Events News Ways to Give toggle menu Apply Now Visit Us Request Info Academics Expand Submenu Explore All Programs Academic Departments Courses & Registration Education Abroad Internships & Co-ops Co-curricular Programs Online Programs Academic Support Devereaux Library Museum of Geology Admissions & Aid Expand Submenu Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions International Students Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Mines Contact Admissions Student Life Expand Submenu Living On Campus Opportunity Center Health & Safety Support & Services Campus Points of Interest Get Involved Research & Innovation Expand Submenu Research Research Facilities Innovation & Entrepreneurship Industry Engagement Athletics Expand Submenu About Expand Submenu Accreditation State Authorization Mission, Vision, & Values Strategic Plan Campus Points of Interest History & Traditions Points of Pride University Leadership Offices & Administration Safety & Security Faculty & Staff Directory Policies & Compliance I am a Current Student Admitted Student Faculty/Staff Parent/Family Alumni Industry Partner Events News Ways to Give toggle search search submit Expand actions Apply Now Visit Us Request Info Internships and Co-ops Home student-life support-and-services career-services Internships and Co-ops At South Dakota Mines, learning goes beyond the classroom. Hands-on experience is\n               the hallmark of a Hardrocker education, and our internship and co-op program connects\n               students with leading employers across the nation. In the 2024-2025 academic year, 75% of graduates reported having a paid, real-world experience during their time at Mines.\n                  These opportunities help students build skills, expand networks, and often lead directly\n                  to full-time job offers. Through internships, co-ops, and research, Mines students apply classroom knowledge\n                  to real challenges at companies like Garmin, Google, Caterpillar, and Nucor — gaining\n                  the expertise and confidence that make them among the most sought-after graduates\n                  in the country. Career Services at South Dakota Mines advocates for all students to receive paid internship\n                     and co-op opportunities in alignment with NACE's position statement on unpaid internships . Internship Search - Online Resources: Handshake Idealist Glassdoor YouTern Chegg Internships HER Campus SimplyHired Internships USA LinkedIn Indeed.com Global Experiences NASA Pathways Program CollegeGrad Internships HACU Nat'l Internship Program Internship Programs USA Jobs Internships Intern Jobs Way Up Internships Co-op Documents Academic Credit Job Offer Form Evaluation Student Report Format back to top 501 E. Saint Joseph St. Rapid City, SD 57701 (605) 394-2511 admissions@sdsmt.edu Consumer Information Directory Careers at Mines Campus Map Sustainability © South Dakota Mines Site design by iFactory ©"
    },
    "https://www.sdsmt.edu/about/offices-and-administration/human-resources/careers-at-mines.html": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers at Mines Skip to content I am a Current Student Admitted Student Faculty/Staff Parent/Family Alumni Industry Partner Events News Ways to Give toggle menu Apply Now Visit Us Request Info Academics Expand Submenu Explore All Programs Academic Departments Courses & Registration Education Abroad Internships & Co-ops Co-curricular Programs Online Programs Academic Support Devereaux Library Museum of Geology Admissions & Aid Expand Submenu Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions International Students Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Mines Contact Admissions Student Life Expand Submenu Living On Campus Opportunity Center Health & Safety Support & Services Campus Points of Interest Get Involved Research & Innovation Expand Submenu Research Research Facilities Innovation & Entrepreneurship Industry Engagement Athletics Expand Submenu About Expand Submenu Accreditation State Authorization Mission, Vision, & Values Strategic Plan Campus Points of Interest History & Traditions Points of Pride University Leadership Offices & Administration Safety & Security Faculty & Staff Directory Policies & Compliance I am a Current Student Admitted Student Faculty/Staff Parent/Family Alumni Industry Partner Events News Ways to Give toggle search search submit Expand actions Apply Now Visit Us Request Info Careers at South Dakota Mines Section Menu Home about offices-and-administration human-resources Careers at Mines Section Menu Close navigation menu offices-and-administration Careers at Mines Benefits Careers at Mines Join more than 425 faculty and staff whose impact is felt on campus, in the community,\n                     and the world beyond. In this rich environment of innovation and education, you'll\n                     experience growth and effect change. Explore our job opportunities and discover a\n                     breadth of exciting careers. Employment Opportunities Faculty & Staff South Dakota Mines in conjunction with the South Dakota Board of Regents utilizes\n               an online shared employment system for all of our employee recruitment efforts. This\n               system allows applicants to search vacancies, complete online applications, and attach\n               application materials. Click the button below, then choose “South Dakota Mines” from\n               the search list. Search Employment Opportunities For more information on benefits, visit the following page: Benefits Non-State Positions at South Dakota Mines Including Sodexo (dining services), South Dakota Mines Center for Alumni Relations\n               and Advancement (CARA) Employment Opportunities for Students Student Employment : Work-Study and Non-Work-Study opportunities. Resources For Employers You can connect with our exceptional engineering and science students through our\n                     Career Services Office. Visit South Dakota Mines Career Services online resources to find out more about recruiting on campus, career fairs, and more. Email: careerservices@sdsmt.edu Phone: (605) 394-2667 back to top 501 E. Saint Joseph St. Rapid City, SD 57701 (605) 394-2511 admissions@sdsmt.edu Consumer Information Directory Careers at Mines Campus Map Sustainability © South Dakota Mines Site design by iFactory ©"
